.TH OPENVPN3-TUI 1 "October 2026" "OpenVPN 3 TUI 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openvpn3-tui \- terminal interface for OpenVPN 3 Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openvpn3-tui
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage OpenVPN profiles and sessions from a local console, VM console,
terminal emulator or SSH. A graphical desktop is not required.
Use the account that owns the OpenVPN profiles. Running with sudo changes
the identity and profiles available to the client.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Simulate profiles and commands without changing real VPN connections.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.SH KEYS
Arrow keys select a profile or session. Enter or C connects; D disconnects;
P pauses or resumes; I imports; N renames; X deletes; E exports with
owner-only permissions. V shows identifiers; S shows raw statistics;
L opens logs; A opens all installed CLI commands and options.
Slash searches; R refreshes; exclamation mark shows the full notification;
question mark shows help; Q quits.
.PP
The command builder supports searchable options, repeated flags, optional
values, and redacted previews. Escape cancels prompts. Ctrl+U clears input.
Passwords entered in secret option fields are masked and not persisted.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Commands temporarily take over the terminal for passwords, MFA, and other
OpenVPN prompts. Ctrl+C stops a command; Enter returns to the dashboard.
Output stays visible until you return. The app does not record credentials
or command output. Terminal scrollback remains controlled by your terminal.
.SH NOTES
Requires a curses-capable terminal of at least 80 columns and 24 rows.
Traffic is sampled for the selected connected session every two seconds.
Rates are derived from transport byte counters, including VPN overhead.
Charts use ASCII intensity levels and cover the last 60 seconds sampled.
.PP
Closing the client does not disconnect established sessions. A stopped CLI
command may have already changed session state; refresh before retrying.
Do not disconnect a VPN that carries your own remote administration session
unless you have another way to reach the server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openvpn3 (1),
.BR openvpn3-gui (1)
